nio: skip the secure-root check after mounting

The photograph of run 593 is decisive: the RAMDisk root mounts
successfully -- "BSD root: md0" and "ROOT mount OK" are both on
the panel -- and then the boot stops before VFS_ROOT, devfs or
load_init_program.

Right after vfs_mountroot(), bsd_init() calls IOSecureBSDRoot().
Despite its name it is not a check on this board: it waits up to
30 tick-seconds for a matched IOPlatformExpert and then asserts
that it found one.  The matching runs on its own thread now, the
clock is not ticking yet, so the deadline never arrives and the
boot stops here with the root already mounted.

The root is the mockfs image in the RAM disk; there is no
SecureRootName to verify.  Return before the wait.  This is the
last of the tick-based waits on the path to launchd.

diff --git a/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp b/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
index 2c1b0b1..6c9a289 100644
--- a/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
@@ -1072,6 +1072,15 @@ void
 IOSecureBSDRoot(const char * rootName)
 {
 #if CONFIG_SECURE_BSD_ROOT
+	/* nio: the root is the mockfs image in the RAM disk (md0), mounted
+	 * by vfs_mountroot just before this call.  There is no SecureRootName
+	 * to check, and the lookup below waits 30 tick-seconds for a matched
+	 * IOPlatformExpert; the clock is not ticking yet and the matching now
+	 * runs on its own thread, so that wait never ends and the boot stops
+	 * after the root is mounted.  Skip the check -- nothing to secure. */
+	IOLog("nio: skip IOSecureBSDRoot\n");
+	return;
+
 	IOReturn         result;
 	IOPlatformExpert *pe;
 	OSDictionary     *matching;
